5 — Canonical consent format & signing (exact, copy/paste)

Canonical string (versioned):

consent_v1|role|fileSHA256|conversationId|messageId|partyIdHash|ISO_ts


Where:

role = "sender" or "receiver"

fileSHA256 = hex lowercase of raw file bytes (not base64)

partyIdHash = SHA256(userId) (hex) — avoid raw user id on-chain

ISO_ts = timestamp like 2025-11-14T18:00:00Z

Compute & sign (client):

canonical = "consent_v1|sender|..."

H = SHA256(canonical) → 32-byte hex (0x prefixed for on-chain)

sig = Sign_Ed25519(H) (signature encoded base64 or hex)

POST {messageId, conversationId, fileSHA256, consentHash: H, signature: sig, ts} to POST /api/files/upload/suspicious

Verify (backend):

Recompute H locally from provided metadata (server gets partyIdHash and other fields).

Verify sig using the uploader’s identityPublicKey.

If verified → accept and create suspicious record and enqueue anchor job.

